dim M_2(Gamma_0(5)) = 1   dim S_2 = 0
M_2(Gamma_1(5)) split by character  [order, char, dim M_2, dim S_2]: [[1, Mod(1, 5), 1, 0], [2, Mod(4, 5), 2, 0]]
  => trivial char: dim 1 (E_{2,5});  quadratic char chi_5: dim 2, all Eisenstein.
dim M_2(Gamma_0(5),chi_5) = 2

higher levels on the same t-line (trivial character), dim M_2 / dim S_2:
  N = 5:  1 / 0
  N = 10:  3 / 0
  N = 15:  4 / 1
  N = 20:  6 / 1
  N = 25:  5 / 0

Gamma_0(5)+5 has ONE cusp, so every weight-0 modular unit with cuspidal divisor
has divisor 0 and is constant: the family F -> F*U is empty on this host.
On Gamma_0(5) (two cusps) the unit is u=(eta_5/eta_1)^6, but a weight-2 form has
divisor of degree mu/6 = 1, so ord_oo(E_{2,5}*u^j) = j forces j = 0.
